{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T06:33:10.936Z","ordinal":2459,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0760c2a023788e66016ab37287bbe487d18fe57b6c7a0836c3","status":"completed","call_id":"call_qS0LIqhWv59TF9gCOROPCfC2","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/ubuntu/cd3-cpu-work/docs/cd3-cpu-path.md\\n+# CD3 CSR CPU path\\n+\\n+Both performance suites accept `--cd3-kv-cpu-path legacy|optimized` (default:\\n+`optimized`). Standalone callers set `TIERED_SERVE_KV_CD3_CPU_PATH`. Garbage\\n+policy remains a separate option, `--cd3-kv-csr-policy append|compact|reuse`,\\n+whose default is still `append`.\\n+\\n+The optimized path makes three changes without changing the codec, attention,\\n+paired serial decoder, dedicated KV budget, or GPU staging capacity:\\n+\\n+1. Allocate CSR entries and offsets directly in pinned memory. Calling\\n+   `torch.empty(...).pin_memory()` allocates pageable storage first and copies\\n+   its entire contents into a second allocation, including unused capacity.\\n+2. Prepare serial CSR routing once per decode-plan generation. One native\\n+   object owns the sources, compact offset snapshots, and descriptors for both\\n+   GPU rings. Adjacent body slots are merged; each side's offsets use one copy.\\n+   Submission still uses one combined CUDA batch. For B body spans and E\\n+   nonempty entries arrays, non-repacked descriptors fall from `4B + 1 + E` to\\n+   `2B + 3 + E`, with the same bytes. Repacked layouts already have compact\\n+   offsets. Multiple decode chunks retain separate reusable plans.\\n+3. Rebuild persistent CSR from live packed ranges. Physically adjacent retained\\n+   ranges share a memcpy. Updated slots always come from fresh encoder scratch,\\n+   including same-size overwrites. Fresh destination storage preserves older\\n+   H2D readers. Native code validates bounds and overlapping inputs before\\n+   publishing new offsets/counts. Retired zero-count rows may have stale offsets\\n+   and are ignored.\\n+\\n+These mechanisms apply to arbitrary valid slot layouts and request sequences.\\n+There are no model/trace-specific thresholds. No additional GPU kernel or\\n+normal-path synchronization is introduced. The existing generation, worker,\\n+and H2D completion rules continue to control source lifetime and slot reuse.\\n+The `legacy` setting retains the previous allocation, scratch repacking, and\\n+serial submission paths for controlled comparisons.\\n+\\n+## Diagnostics\\n+\\n+`--cd3-cpu-profile` enables bounded host elapsed-time counters and writes\\n+`cd3_cpu_profile.<pid>.json` under the cell's `kv_metrics` directory. Serving\\n+automatically enables byte counters. The manifest marks diagnostic performance\\n+metrics invalid; run again without CPU profiling for latency comparisons.\\n+CPU profiling adds no GPU timing events or synchronization. Storage, retirement,\\n+and worker categories apply to both execution modes; detailed native transfer\\n+API and GIL categories currently cover CSR serial execution.\\n+\\n+Categories overlap: rebuild is included in retirement/free or worker time, and\\n+workers run concurrently. API elapsed time may include driver waits or GPU\\n+backpressure. Do not add categories or interpret API time as CPU cycles.\\n+Byte counters cover all server forwards, while client request trimming applies\\n+only to client latency statistics.\\n+\\n+## Representative serving comparison\\n+\\n+Run in the container repository with the cached Llama-3.1-70B model:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+bash scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n+  --codecs cd3 --modes kvcomp \\\\\\n+  --cd3-kv-storage csr --cd3-kv-csr-policy compact \\\\\\n+  --cd3-kv-execution serial --cd3-kv-cpu-path optimized \\\\\\n+  --chunks 8192 --request-rates 4 --max-num-seqs 64 \\\\\\n+  --dedicated-kv-blocks 2432 --num-prompts 192 \\\\\\n+  --skip-first-n-requests 16 --skip-last-n-requests 16 \\\\\\n+  --repeats 1 --kv-byte-metrics \\\\\\n+  --output-root benchmark_results/cd3_cpu/compact\\n+```\\n+\\n+Use the same byte-counter setting for both sides. To compare another request\\n+cohort, `--dataset-path PATH` passes an Azure CSV through the existing serving\\n+client. It does not replace serving with a replay of compressor operations.\\n+See [measured results](cd3-cpu-results.md) for conditions, limits, and artifacts.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"docker cp /home/ubuntu/cd3-cpu-work/docs/cd3-cpu-path.md tiered-serve:/root/projects/tiered-serve/docs/cd3-cpu-path.md\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"tail -6 /home/ubuntu/cd3-cpu-work/train-packed-compact.log\",max_output_tokens:1300}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0ccc1-54b0-7be0-97d5-272ff0bcc061","create_time":1790145148.398188}}}
